# Pilot blocker: the protected resource is the Iris MCP URL, and the API issuer must not derive from it. 2026-09-13
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/olympus-platform.git wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-13-resource-is-iris.plan --auto --retries 1
#
# Observed on the first real connection (host B, 2026-09-13 10:49 local): the host
# fetched /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server on the IRIS origin (404) and then
# GET /authorize on Iris (404). It ignored our protected resource metadata because
# its resource field names the API (.../api/v1/assistant) while the host requires
# it to equal the MCP server URL exactly as typed (https://olympus-iris-...run.app/mcp).
# Fixing the resource alone breaks the API issuer, which W2-A round three tied to
# the origin of ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI. Both must change together.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | go-backend | Branch fix/ac-resource-is-iris. READ FIRST docs/prd/pages/assistant-channel.md section 6 (host B row: resource must match the MCP URL as typed), docs/operations/assistant-hosts.md preflight item 5, apps/api/internal/handler/assistant_oauth.go (assistantMetadataOrigin, the issuer and authorization_servers derivation, audience validation), apps/api/internal/middleware/auth.go (WithAssistantAudience), apps/api/internal/config/config.go (ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI, OLYMPUS_API_URL or the public base URL the API already knows), and services/iris (cmd/iris/main.go config, the protected resource metadata, the issuer parity check from round three, token audience check). DELIVER: ONE, in the API the issuer and the authorization-server metadata origin come from the API public base URL (the config value the API already uses for its own absolute URLs; add ASSISTANT_ISSUER only if no such value exists, documented), never from ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI. TWO, ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI means the protected resource, which is the Iris MCP endpoint (IRIS_PUBLIC_URL plus /mcp); the API validates the resource parameter on authorize and token against it and mints it as aud; the middleware requires that aud. THREE, in Iris the protected resource metadata resource field equals IRIS_PUBLIC_URL plus /mcp exactly, authorization_servers stays the API origin, and the token audience check expects the same resource value; the round-three parity check now asserts that the API issuer equals OLYMPUS_API_URL and that ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI equals the Iris MCP URL, refusing to boot otherwise; update the critic parity test to the new rule. FOUR, tests: discovery document on the API carries issuer equal to the API origin while resource is the Iris URL; an access token minted for the Iris resource passes the API middleware and the Iris check; one minted for any other aud fails both. VERIFY: go test ./... with the race flag in apps/api and services/iris, real exit codes pasted. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR with Refs 2800 and 2340, and state the two env changes the operator must apply (ASSISTANT_RESOURCE_URI on both services becomes the Iris MCP URL). | fix/ac-resource-is-iris

